  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protecting Livelihoods Assets Through Provision of Humanitarian Assistance in Cyclone Affected Coastal Areas.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to protect the livelihoods and agriculture assets of 10,800 farming households in the coastal districts of Bangladesh. This FAO project provides cash grants to farming households to help relocate their livelihood assets. Nutrient-rich animal feed will also be distributed. The project targets a total of 54,000 people, including 13,500 women, 13,500 men, 27,000 children, and 1,512 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
